Subject: GGIR version 2.0 on CRAN
Message-ID: <8EYEX3ICQU8.hQGoGd2cBwAJ@rpackageggir.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rpackageggir/c/8EYEX3ICQU8/m/hQGoGd2cBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GGIR version 2.0 is now on CRAN.

Main updates:
- GGIR now facilitates external function embedding, enabling you to apply your own R/Python functions to the raw data while benefiting from the existing data handling framework https://bit.ly/2YqBFJF <https://t.co/1E0BBVNwyL?amp=1>.
- GGIR’s sleep estimates are now better fed into its time-use analysis. Output variable names for both have been revised to be more intuitive and documentation has been expanded https://bit.ly/3fgQkNE <https://t.co/AaJjoe04HY?amp=1>.
- GGIR’s package vignette now clarifies how to use published intensity cut-points from various data metrics, for hip and wrist-worn accelerometer data collected in a variety of age groups https://bit.ly/2xsrYzj <https://t.co/RnP0vnhjv3?amp=1>.

See change log <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/GGIR/news.html> for full overview.

