> By default g.cwaread uses the local timezone of the machine where the data is processed. So, if you happen to be in a different timezone than where the data was collected you will need to provide the timezone explicitly to g.cwaread and when you generate the timestamp. The best way to verify that you are doing it right is by making a test recording for which you know the exact start and end time.

